# No ad-hoc regen scaffolding

Do **not** create parallel "regen", "refresh", "tmp", or one-off paper/figure scripts that re-call plot functions and write the same curated outputs as the real pipeline.

## Forbidden

- `scripts/regen_*.py`, `scripts/tmp_*.py`, `_regen_*.py`, notebook cells, or chat-only scripts whose job is "replot X into paper/figures"
- Any second entrypoint that duplicates `visualize.py` / experiment plot code and can overwrite already-correct artifacts
- Bundling unrelated figures into one regen so fixing trajectories silently clobbers activation heatmaps (or vice versa)

## Required instead

1. Change the **canonical** plot function / CLI (`visualize.py`, experiment runners, etc.).
2. Replot via that entrypoint (add `--only` / flags if missing — do not invent a sibling pipeline).
3. If curated copies exist (e.g. `paper/figures/`), update **one** collect/sync mapping that copies/converts from experiment outputs — never regenerates plots itself.
4. Prefer editing existing collect manifests over adding new scripts.

## Why

Throwaway regen scripts caused correct paper figures to be overwritten with wrong parameters. That is unacceptable. Fix the real path once.
